				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">for darnok mostly, but writing this in generel board so that perhaps others can benefit from it.
<br />

<br />
MPG drop list 
<br />
Drop list for the single group trials:
<br />

<br />
Fear: 
<br />
ID 01: Supple Crimson Choker
<br />
ID 02: Facade of Fright
<br />
ID 03: Despair
<br />

<br />
Weaponry:
<br />
ID 04: Sash of the Battlemaster 
<br />
ID 05: Painbringer's Velvet Pelisse 
<br />
ID 06: Signet of the Armsman
<br />

<br />
Subversion:
<br />
ID 07: Stalker's Shoulderguards
<br />
ID 08: Emblem of the False Priestess 
<br />
ID 09: Bauble of Premonitions
<br />

<br />
Efficiency: 
<br />
ID 10: Eyepatch of Efficiency
<br />
ID 11: Girdle of Efficiency
<br />
ID 12: Rime-Encrusted Greatstaff
<br />

<br />
Ingenuity: 
<br />
ID 13: Strategist's Indigo Cloak 
<br />
ID 14: Clockwork Talisman of Invention
<br />
ID 15: Bane of the Stonegazer
<br />

<br />
Destruction: 
<br />
ID 16: Horn of Doomcalling
<br />
ID 17: Tri-Spined Spaulders of Destruction
<br />
ID 18: Eye of the Lightninglord
<br />

<br />
<a href="http://lucy.allakhazam.com/item.html?id=70601" target="_blank">http://lucy.allakhazam.com/item.html?id=70601</a>
<br />

<br />
use the above link and alter the number to the id matching the item you want to check out, ie. id=70616 = horn of doomcalling.
<br />

<br />
as the post states, these are one group trials. when you complete a trial, an aa skill called trials of meta'muram is added to your OoW aa skill tray at 0 cost, you gain 1 rank per trial you win. for each rank your maximum resists are upped by 8, so with all 6 trials, level 70 and 5 aa's in resists, you can get 598 resists which is pretty neat.
<br />

<br />
in generel about the difficulty;
<br />
all of the trials involve time pressure, either there's a total time limit to complete a set task, or timers for new waves etc.
<br />
the trials are in many ways compareable to the justice trials and the ikkinz 1-3 (singular might, twins, tri-fates), in the beginning it's very recomendable to be very selective with what classes you bring to which trials. 
<br />
for example, for the trial of fear, you would probably want a necro, an enchanter, a cleric, a warrior/pal/sk , a druid/ranger (depending on how good the cleric/war is), and a rogue (consistant dps non-dependant on mana), 
<br />
while for the trial of power, you would want to bring a war/pal/sk, cleric, shm/enc (shm can be adviseable, depending on tank quality as far from all the adds are mezzable), rog, rog, rog (others are fine too, but mobs are very spell resistant, so consistant melee dps is an advantage).
<br />

<br />
anyway, the point is, that they can be done easily enough with "odd" classes if everyone in the group is familiar with the trial, but do start with a good setup.
<br />

<br />
the trials are located in muramite proving grounds, about as far away from the entrence as they can possibly be (there's a good map on mapfiend), but you can usually invis up to around riftseekers niveau saving 10-20 mins clearing. 
<br />
   you get the trial from a "projection of &lt;&gt;"... mind ie. for the fear trial.
<br />
once you complete a trial (or fail, god forbid it), you get 90 mins lockout for all the trials, not just the one you won.
<br />

<br />
each trial yield one of the above loots, some seems more rare than others, but there's no generel pattern (you cant say: the one with the lowest id is the most common etc.), and rarely (30% or so) a 69-70 rune.
<br />

<br />
on a sidenote, the raid version of these trials, are somewhat harder, and allthough they are not all 100% gear-dependable, i do not recommend going there with sub-time gear(but some of the single group ones, especially fear, can be done with elemental gear with the right group setup/tactic without too much difficulty.).
<br />

<br />
det var vidst det... jeg raider med guilden fra 15.00-1700 ca. før jeg tager afsted, ellers ses vi næste weekend først :/, håber at i kan hitte ud af dem, ellers spørg ind. Det er vildt nok at der dropper "quarm" items fra 1 gruppe trials, men hvem ved om der kommer et nerf snart <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="Smile" border="0" /></span><span class="postbody"><br />_________________<br />Myrian.
